      ⍝ Bugs11 regression tests (Blake McBride, 2026-08-04)
      ⍝
      ⍝ #1: ⎕MX[6] (ident) with negative B used to build a Value with an
      ⍝ uninitialized ravel (Shape(¯N,¯N) has a positive volume) instead
      ⍝ of rejecting it -- fatal on printing the result.
      ⍝
      ⎕MX[6] ¯5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕MX[6]¯5
      ^

      ⎕MX[6] ¯1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕MX[6]¯1
      ^

      ⍝ #2: ⎕MX[4]/[5] (eigenvector/eigenvalue) on an empty square matrix
      ⍝ used to call gsl_eigen_nonsymmv_alloc(0), which aborts the whole
      ⍝ interpreter via GSL's default error handler.
      ⍝
      ⎕MX[4] 0 0⍴0
LENGTH ERROR+
      ⎕MX[4]0 0⍴0
      ^

      ⎕MX[5] 0 0⍴0
LENGTH ERROR+
      ⎕MX[5]0 0⍴0
      ^

      ⍝ #3: ⎕MX[1] (determinant) of a 1×1 matrix used to return 0 instead
      ⍝ of the single element (getDet() had no rows()==1 base case).
      ⍝
      ⎕MX[1] 1 1⍴5
5

      ⍝ #4: the 100...103 axes (documented shorthands for ⎕MX[10, D])
      ⍝ were unreachable monadically and in the vector-X form of the
      ⍝ dyadic case, because the subfun_count range check treated the
      ⍝ .def row count as a maximum axis number; axis 104 was also
      ⍝ wrongly registered for t_dist (should be 103, and 104 is not a
      ⍝ valid axis at all). Verify: 104 is correctly rejected, and a
      ⍝ shorthand axis is equivalent to its ⎕MX[10, D] expansion.
      ⍝
      3 ⎕MX[104] 1.5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      3 ⎕MX[104]1.5
      ^ ^
      )MORE
A ⎕MX[X] B: invalid subfunction number X (= 104).
See: ⎕MX '' or: ⎕MX ⍬ for a list of valid numbers.

      ⊣⎕MX[14] 7
      Z1←⎕MX[100] 1 2 3
      ⊣⎕MX[14] 7
      Z2←⎕MX[10 0] 1 2 3
      Z1≡Z2
1

      ⍝ chi-squared and student-t (dist 2 and 3) require a strictly
      ⍝ positive degrees-of-freedom parameter; B≤0 used to be undefined
      ⍝ behaviour (observed as corrupt, non-UTF8 output) instead of a
      ⍝ clean error -- found while verifying #4, not one of Blake's
      ⍝ numbered findings.
      ⍝
      3 ⎕MX[10 2] 0
DOMAIN ERROR+
      3 ⎕MX[10 2]0
      ^ ^

      3 ⎕MX[10 3] ¯1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      3 ⎕MX[10 3]¯1
      ^ ^

      ⍝ clear the SI left behind by the DOMAIN/LENGTH ERRORs above
      ⍝
      )SIC


